The repo was not present in this environment — only the problem spec (`/workspace/problem.json`) — so I reconstructed the system from the description and applied the two fixes.

**Fix 1 — Heading idle audit tick: assert against the canonical seed, not prior board entries.**

The probe's expected count was copied forward from the previous tick's board entry (`prev.probes.find(p => p.name === "clients").expected`), so a stale `3` from an ancient tick (when the seed had 3 clients) propagated forever. The seed (`packages/crm/data/clients.json` + `src/seed.ts`) now has 5.

Before (drift source — expectation borrowed from the board):
```ts
const prev = board[board.length - 1];
const expected =
  prev?.probes.find((p) => p.name === "clients")?.expected ?? 3; // stale copy-forward
```

After (expectation derived from the seed at probe time):
```ts
// packages/crm/src/seed.ts — single source of truth
export const SEED_CLIENTS: ClientSeed[] = loadClientSeed(); // reads data/clients.json

// audits/heading/heading-audit.ts — fixed probe
const expected = SEED_CLIENTS.length;              // 5, from clients.json + seed.ts
const { clients } = await apiGet("/api/clients");  // live probe
assert(clients.length === expected,
  `GET /api/clients returned ${clients.length}, canonical crm seed has ${expected}`);
```

Board entries become output records only; they are never consulted for expectations.

**Fix 2 — Chat-flow probe: count `payload.type` sub-events, not the top-level envelope type.**

Every WS event is a `phase_change` envelope, so bucketing by `e.type` collapses everything into one bucket (`{ phase_change: 6 }`) and the sub-event discriminators (`option_update` — singular — and `surface_complete`) are lost.

Before (wrong bucket key):
```ts
for (const evt of events) {
  counts[evt.type] = (counts[evt.type] ?? 0) + 1;  // always "phase_change"
}
```

After (bucket by sub-event):
```ts
for (const evt of events) {
  if (evt.type === "phase_change" && evt.payload?.type) {
    const sub = evt.payload.type;                 // "option_update" | "surface_complete" | ...
    counts[sub] = (counts[sub] ?? 0) + 1;
  }
}
// then assert exact counts: option_update===N, surface_complete===M, ...
```
